 UPI Fraud Detection & Transaction Monitoring Dashboard

 Project Overview

This project explores UPI transaction patterns using Python, MySQL, and Power BI. It focuses on analysing transaction behaviour, identifying potential anomalies, and presenting insights through an interactive dashboard.

 Objectives

- Analyse transaction amounts, timings, locations, and merchant categories.
- Explore potential transaction anomalies using IQR and Isolation Forest.
- Query transaction data using MySQL.
- Visualise key metrics and transaction patterns in Power BI.

 Tools & Technologies
- Python
- Pandas
- MySQL
- Power BI
- DAX
- Data Visualisation
- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

 Dataset
The project uses 10,000 synthetic UPI transactions. The dataset contains 300 transactions labelled as fraudulent (3%) and 9,700 labelled as legitimate.

Dashboard Features
- Total transaction and fraud-labelled transaction KPIs
- Fraud rate analysis
- Transaction trends by hour
- Merchant category analysis
- Filters for location, transaction type, and merchant category

 Project Files
The repository contains the analysis notebook, SQL queries, dashboard files, screenshots, and dataset where available.

 Key Learning Outcomes
- Data analysis and exploratory analysis
- SQL querying and data handling
- Anomaly exploration
- KPI reporting and Power BI dashboard development

